Based on the analysis of the error log and source code, the root cause is a logic error in the `fcb_new_sector` function in `subsys/fs/fcb/fcb_append.c`. The `do-while` loop iterates one time too many due to the use of post-increment (`i++`) in the loop condition. This causes an incorrect check against the oldest sector, leading to a premature out-of-space error (`-ENOSPC`).

The test `test_fcb_append_fill` fails because it's unable to switch to the second sector after filling the first one. Consequently, `elem_cnts[0]` contains the number of entries in the first sector, while `elem_cnts[1]` remains 0, causing the assertion `elem_cnts[0] == elem_cnts[1]` to fail.

The fix is to change the post-increment `i++` to a pre-increment `++i` in the loop condition. This corrects the number of loop iterations to `cnt + 1`, ensuring that the correct number of subsequent sectors are checked for availability without incorrectly including an extra sector that might be the oldest one.

